# fullcell_tall (2026-09-29): the SEI-morphology box. 20 x 20 x 100 cells =
# 8 x 8 x 40 nm, 640000 sites (13x fullcell_physical). Same anode slab
# (40.4 A) and one BC layer of S8 (400 sites, 6400 Li demand); the anode is
# backed by a finite foil (li_bulk_init) so that the accelerated SEI does not
# exhaust the Li inventory. cathode_thickness 0.006 x 400 A = 2.4 A = one BC
# layer, as 0.02 x 120 A was in the small box.
# fullcell_physical: anode slab 40.4 A (~2200 Li, the whole Li inventory since
# li_bulk_init 0) against one BC layer of S8 (100 sites, 1600 Li demand):
# N/P ~ 1.4. fullcell_cei used 20.2 A / 700 sites (N/P 0.10, semi-infinite foil).
# cathode_center 0.0 -> the S8 slab wraps both z faces (periodic band)
latticeConstant 4.0
nx 20
ny 20
nz 100
anode_center 0.5
anode_thickness_A 40.4
anode_thickness_is_fraction false
anode_species Li
cathode_enabled true
cathode_species S8
cathode_center 0.0
cathode_thickness 0.006
cathode_charge 0
cathode_access_fraction 1.0
write_poscar false
# ---- dynamic passivation by the CEI film (milestone 2) ---------------------
# [SF26]: the sulfite/thiosulfate/LiF film is electronically insulating and
# passivates the cathode. Film sites occupy the electrolyte (OC/BA) shell of a
# cathode site, which holds 18 to 22 of its 26 neighbours. nmin 10 = a cathode
# site is blocked once about half of its electrolyte-facing shell is film
# (geometric threshold, PLACEHOLDER; no literature value exists for a lattice
# criterion). Li16S8 (= Li2S, wide-gap insulator) and Li8S8 (= Li2S2) block as in the
# original point 3; the CEI film species block per [SF26].
cathode_passivating_species Li16S8,Li8S8,CEI_SOx,CEI_org
cathode_passivation_nmin 10
